{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/i3ccr8","slideIndex":1,"text":"Source: Figure 22, assets/human-practices/images/shahe-needs-assessment-and-workbook-feedback.png, especially older-adult information habits, workbook changes and AI use. Larger type summarizes the reported problem of small print. More pictures, fewer words, space for notes and production budget come directly from the workbook panel. Everyday health questions reflect health-knowledge needs and note-taking in that panel, also described in docs/human-practices/human-practices.md. Familiar short-video platforms and primarily voice-based AI interactions come from the same source. The source is a Shahe Elderly Service Center fieldwork summary; it does not establish that the institution is an elderly university. “Older learners” avoids changing the institution’s identity. These are feedback and design directions, not demonstrated educational outcomes."}